{"t": 1794109219.3936152, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "*AG-7731 PaymentGatewayErrors checkout \u2014 root cause found*\n\n*Cause:* The payment gateway switched to API 2026-11 at 07:41 UTC, which enforces \"strict amounts\": `amount` must be an integer in minor units (cents). `checkout/gateway.py` was still sending decimal euros, so charges were rejected with HTTP 400 `invalid_amount` (e.g. `got 12.34`), driving the 38% gateway 4xx rate.\n\n*Fix:* `charge_payload()` now converts EUR to integer cents (12.34 -> 1234) using Decimal with half-up rounding. Verified locally for representative amounts; no other callers in the repo.\n\n*Next:* deploy checkout with the fix and watch the gateway 4xx rate. If errors persist, check whether other services still send decimal amounts."}, "ok": true}
